UPDATE schemes SET `content`='<p>PM Kisan Samman Nidhi Yojana is a flagship central government scheme launched in February 2019 by the Ministry of Agriculture and Farmers Welfare. The scheme aims to provide direct income support of Rs 6,000 per year to small and marginal farmers across India. This financial assistance is transferred directly to the bank accounts of eligible farmers in three equal installments of Rs 2,000 each, helping them meet agricultural expenses and improve their livelihood.</p><h2>Objectives of the Scheme</h2><p>The primary objective of PM Kisan Yojana is to supplement the financial needs of small and marginal farmers in procuring various inputs to ensure proper crop health and yield. The scheme also aims to protect farmers from falling into the debt trap of moneylenders and ensure a steady income flow for their agricultural activities.</p><h2>Eligibility Criteria</h2><p>All small and marginal farmers who own less than 2 hectares of cultivable land are eligible for this scheme. The scheme covers farmers irrespective of their caste, religion, gender or community. Landless farmers who cultivate land on lease are also eligible provided they have valid cultivation documents. However, former and current government employees, income tax payers, and professionals like doctors and engineers are not eligible for the scheme.</p><h2>Benefits and Financial Assistance</h2><p>Eligible farmers receive Rs 6,000 per year in three installments of Rs 2,000 each. The first installment is released between April and July, the second installment between August and November, and the third installment between December and March. The amount is directly credited to the Aadhaar-linked bank account of the beneficiary through Direct Benefit Transfer (DBT) mechanism, ensuring transparency and eliminating middlemen.</p><h2>How to Apply</h2><p>Farmers can apply through multiple channels. They can visit the official website pmkisan.gov.in and register under the Farmers Corner section. Alternatively, they can visit their nearest Common Service Centre (CSC) or approach the local Agriculture Officer or Patwari for assistance with the application process. The application requires basic details including Aadhaar number, land records and bank account information.</p><h2>Documents Required</h2><ul><li>Aadhaar Card (mandatory for identity verification)</li><li>Land documents or cultivation proof from patwari</li><li>Bank account passbook with IFSC code</li><li>Passport size photograph</li><li>Mobile number linked to Aadhaar</li></ul><h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2><h3>Can a farmer with more than 2 hectares apply?</h3><p>No, the scheme is specifically for small and marginal farmers with less than 2 hectares of land.</p><h3>How can I check my payment status?</h3><p>Visit pmkisan.gov.in, click on Farmers Corner, select Beneficiary Status and enter your Aadhaar number or bank account number.</p><h3>What if my Aadhaar is not linked to my bank account?</h3><p>You must link your Aadhaar to your bank account to receive the benefit. Visit your bank branch for assistance.</p>', `eligibility`='<p>Small and marginal farmers with less than 2 hectares of cultivable land. All farmers regardless of caste, religion, gender. Landless farmers with valid cultivation documents on lease are also eligible. NOT eligible: current/former government employees, income tax payers, doctors, engineers, lawyers and other professionals.</p>', `benefits`='<p>Rs 6,000 per year in three equal installments of Rs 2,000 each. First installment April-July, second installment August-November, third installment December-March. Amount credited directly to Aadhaar-linked bank account via DBT. No intermediaries or middlemen involved.</p>', `application_process`='<p>Step 1: Visit pmkisan.gov.in. Step 2: Click on Farmers Corner. Step 3: Select New Farmer Registration. Step 4: Enter your Aadhaar number. Step 5: Fill in land and bank details. Step 6: Submit and note registration number. Alternate method: Visit Common Service Centre (CSC) in your village with documents.</p>', `required_documents`='<ul><li>Aadhaar Card</li><li>Land Records (Khasra/Khatauni)</li><li>Bank Account Passbook</li><li>Passport Size Photo</li><li>Mobile Number</li></ul>' WHERE `slug`='pm-kisan-samman-nidhi';
UPDATE schemes SET `content`='<p>Pradhan Mantri Fasal Bima Yojana (PMFBY) is a flagship crop insurance scheme launched in 2016 by the Ministry of Agriculture and Farmers Welfare. The scheme provides affordable crop insurance to farmers against crop failure due to natural calamities, pests and diseases. It aims to stabilize farm income and encourage farmers to adopt modern agricultural practices by reducing their financial risk.</p><h2>Coverage</h2><p>The scheme covers all food crops, oilseeds and annual commercial or horticultural crops. It provides coverage against yield losses due to natural fire, lightning, storm, hailstorm, cyclone, typhoon, flood, inundation, drought, dry spells, pests and diseases. Post-harvest losses are also covered for up to 14 days.</p><h2>Premium</h2><p>The premium rates are very affordable: 2% of sum insured for Kharif crops, 1.5% for Rabi crops and 5% for annual commercial or horticultural crops. The difference between the premium paid by farmers and the actual premium is shared by the central and state governments.</p><h2>Eligibility</h2><p>All farmers who have a loan from financial institutions are covered compulsorily. Non-loanee farmers can also voluntarily enroll. Tenant farmers and sharecroppers with valid land records are eligible.</p>', `eligibility`='<p>All farmers including loanee and non-loanee. Tenant farmers and sharecroppers with valid land records eligible. All types of crops covered.</p>', `benefits`='<p>Insurance coverage at nominal premium (2% Kharif, 1.5% Rabi, 5% commercial). Covers yield losses from natural calamities, pests, diseases. Post-harvest loss coverage for 14 days.</p>', `application_process`='<p>Loanee farmers automatically covered through their lending institution. Non-loanee farmers can enroll through Common Service Centres (CSC) or bank branches before the cut-off date for each season.</p>', `required_documents`='<ul><li>Aadhaar Card</li><li>Land Records</li><li>Bank Account Details</li><li>Crop Sowing Details</li></ul>' WHERE `slug`='pm-fasal-bima-yojana';
UPDATE schemes SET `content`='<p>Kisan Credit Card (KCC) scheme was launched in 1998 by the Government of India to provide affordable credit to farmers for their agricultural needs. The scheme is implemented by the Ministry of Agriculture and Farmers Welfare through banks. It provides farmers with timely access to credit for crop production, post-harvest expenses, farm maintenance, dairy and fisheries activities, and other agricultural purposes. The scheme has played a crucial role in reducing farmers dependence on informal money lenders and improving access to institutional credit.</p><h2>Features and Benefits</h2><p>The scheme provides a credit card with a pre-approved limit based on land holding, crop pattern and credit history. Farmers can withdraw cash as needed and pay interest only on the amount used, making it a flexible and cost-effective solution. The card is valid for 5 years with annual renewal, providing continuous access to credit without repeated paperwork. Interest rates are affordable at 7% per annum with an additional 3% subvention for farmers who repay on time, bringing the effective interest rate down to just 4%. This makes it one of the cheapest sources of agricultural credit in India.</p><h2>Coverage and Limits</h2><p>The scheme covers all types of farmers including small, marginal, tenant and sharecroppers. Individual farmers, joint farmers and farmer groups are all eligible. Loans up to Rs 3 lakh are provided with no collateral requirement for loans up to Rs 1.60 lakh. The credit limit is assessed based on the farmers land holding, cropping pattern and scale of farming activities. Personal accident insurance cover of Rs 1 lakh is also provided to cardholders at nominal premium.</p><h2>Eligibility Criteria</h2><p>All farmers including small and marginal farmers, tenant farmers and sharecroppers with valid land records are eligible for the scheme. Individual farmers, joint farmers and farmer producer organizations can apply. Farmers engaged in crop production, dairy farming, fisheries, poultry and other allied activities are covered. There is no upper limit on land holding size for eligibility.</p><h2>Application Process</h2><p>Farmers can apply at any bank branch with their land records and identity proof. The bank assesses the credit limit based on land holding and crop pattern. The assessment takes into account the cost of cultivation, maintenance expenses and family needs. Once approved, the Kisan Credit Card is issued within 15 to 30 days. Farmers can also apply through Common Service Centres and online banking portals.</p><h2>Required Documents</h2><ul><li>Aadhaar Card for identity verification</li><li>Land records or cultivation proof</li><li>Bank account details for loan disbursement</li><li>Passport size photograph</li><li>Crop plan for the upcoming season</li><li>Previous loan repayment history if applicable</li></ul><h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2><h3>Can tenant farmers apply for KCC?</h3><p>Yes, tenant farmers and sharecroppers with valid land records or cultivation certificates are eligible.</p><h3>What is the interest rate on KCC?</h3><p>The interest rate is 7% per annum. Farmers who repay on time get an additional 3% subvention, making the effective rate 4%.</p>', `eligibility`='<p>All farmers including small, marginal, tenant and sharecroppers. Individual and joint farmers. Farmer producer organizations. Farmers engaged in crop, dairy, fisheries and allied activities.</p>', `benefits`='<p>Credit up to Rs 3 lakh at 7% interest. 3% subvention for timely repayment (4% effective rate). No collateral up to Rs 1.60 lakh. Personal accident insurance Rs 1 lakh. 5 year validity with annual renewal.</p>', `application_process`='<p>Apply at any bank branch with land records and identity proof. Bank assesses credit limit based on land holding and crop pattern. Card issued within 15-30 days after verification of documents and credit assessment.</p>', `required_documents`='<ul><li>Aadhaar Card</li><li>Land Records</li><li>Bank Account Details</li><li>Passport Photo</li><li>Crop Plan</li></ul>' WHERE `slug`='kisan-credit-card';
UPDATE schemes SET `content`='<p>Pradhan Mantri Awas Yojana Gramin (PMAY-G) is a central government housing scheme launched in 2015 by the Ministry of Rural Development. The scheme aims to provide pucca houses with basic amenities to all homeless households and families living in kutcha or dilapidated houses in rural areas. The scheme is a key component of the governments Housing for All mission and uses the Socio-Economic and Caste Census (SECC) 2011 database for beneficiary selection.</p><h2>Eligibility</h2><p>Families listed in the SECC 2011 database as houseless or living in kutcha houses are eligible. The scheme covers all rural households including SC, ST, OBC and minority communities. Priority is given to widows, disabled persons, transgenders and families with no adult member aged 18-59 years. Landless families are also eligible provided the state government assigns them land for house construction.</p><h2>Benefits</h2><p>Financial assistance of Rs 1.20 lakh in plain areas and Rs 1.30 lakh in hilly areas for house construction. An additional Rs 12,000 is provided for toilet construction under Swachh Bharat Mission. The house includes basic amenities like electricity, water supply and LPG connection. MGNREGA wages are also integrated for unskilled labor components of house construction.</p><h2>How to Apply</h2><p>Beneficiaries are identified through the SECC database at the Gram Sabha level. Eligible families can also apply to the Gram Panchayat if their name is missing from the list. The Gram Sabha approves the list of beneficiaries and the block development office processes the fund release in installments.</p><h2>Documents Required</h2><ul><li>Aadhaar Card</li><li>SECC inclusion proof or BPL certificate</li><li>Bank account details</li><li>Land ownership document</li><li>Photograph of existing house</li></ul>', `eligibility`='<p>Rural households listed in SECC 2011 as houseless or living in kutcha houses. SC/ST/OBC/minority communities. Priority to widows, disabled, transgenders. Landless families with state-provided land.</p>', `benefits`='<p>Rs 1.20-1.30 lakh for house construction. Rs 12,000 for toilet. Electricity and water supply included. MGNREGA wages integrated. 90 person-days of unskilled labor from MGNREGA.</p>', `application_process`='<p>Beneficiary identification through SECC database. Gram Sabha approval. Block level processing. Fund release in installments based on construction progress monitored by panchayat.</p>', `required_documents`='<ul><li>Aadhaar Card</li><li>SECC/BPL Certificate</li><li>Land Document</li><li>Bank Account</li><li>Existing House Photo</li></ul>' WHERE `slug`='pm-awas-yojana-gramin';
UPDATE schemes SET `content`='<p>Pradhan Mantri Awas Yojana Urban (PMAY-U) is a central government housing scheme launched in June 2015 by the Ministry of Housing and Urban Affairs. The scheme aims to provide pucca houses with basic amenities to all eligible urban households by 2024. It addresses the housing needs of the urban poor including the Economically Weaker Section (EWS), Lower Income Group (LIG) and Middle Income Group (MIG) categories through different verticals of assistance.</p><h2>Four Verticals of PMAY-U</h2><p>The scheme operates through four components: In-Situ Slum Redevelopment (ISSR), Credit Linked Subsidy Scheme (CLSS), Affordable Housing in Partnership (AHP) and Beneficiary Led Individual House Construction (BLIHC). Each vertical targets a specific segment of the urban population with different subsidy amounts and conditions.</p><h2>Eligibility Criteria</h2><p>Applicant families should not own a pucca house anywhere in India. The family should belong to EWS (annual income up to Rs 3 lakh), LIG (Rs 3-6 lakh) or MIG (Rs 6-18 lakh) categories. The scheme is open to all castes, religions and communities. Women ownership or joint ownership is mandatory for EWS and LIG categories. The beneficiary family should not have availed housing subsidy from any other government scheme.</p><h2>Benefits and Subsidy</h2><p>Under CLSS, interest subsidy ranges from 3% to 6.5% on home loans depending on the income category. EWS and LIG get 6.5% subsidy on loans up to Rs 6 lakh. MIG-I gets 4% subsidy on loans up to Rs 9 lakh. MIG-II gets 3% subsidy on loans up to Rs 12 lakh. Under AHP and BLIHC, direct financial assistance of up to Rs 1.5 lakh per house is provided for construction or enhancement.</p><h2>How to Apply</h2><p>Eligible beneficiaries can apply through the official PMAY-U website pmay-urban.gov.in or visit their local municipal corporation or urban local body office. The online portal allows registration, document upload and tracking of application status. Beneficiaries need to provide Aadhaar, income certificate and house ownership documents.</p><h2>Required Documents</h2><ul><li>Aadhaar Card of all family members</li><li>Income certificate from competent authority</li><li>Address proof</li><li>Bank account details for subsidy transfer</li><li>Photograph of existing house</li><li>Property documents if applicable</li></ul>', `eligibility`='<p>Urban households belonging to EWS (income up to Rs 3 lakh), LIG (Rs 3-6 lakh) or MIG (Rs 6-18 lakh). No pucca house anywhere in India. Women ownership mandatory for EWS/LIG. Not availed other housing subsidy.</p>', `benefits`='<p>Interest subsidy of 3% to 6.5% on home loans. Direct assistance up to Rs 1.5 lakh for house construction. Subsidy amount varies by income category. Four different verticals for different needs.</p>', `application_process`='<p>Visit pmay-urban.gov.in or local municipal corporation office. Register with Aadhaar and income details. Upload required documents. Track application status online. Subsidy directly credited to bank account.</p>', `required_documents`='<ul><li>Aadhaar Card</li><li>Income Certificate</li><li>Address Proof</li><li>Bank Account Details</li><li>House Photograph</li><li>Property Documents</li></ul>' WHERE `slug`='pm-awas-yojana-urban';
UPDATE schemes SET `content`='<p>Ayushman Bharat Pradhan Mantri Jan Arogya Yojana (PMJAY) is the worlds largest health insurance scheme launched in September 2018 by the Ministry of Health and Family Welfare. The scheme provides health coverage of Rs 5 lakh per family per year for secondary and tertiary hospitalization to over 55 crore beneficiaries, making it the most ambitious healthcare initiative in the world. The scheme targets the poorest and most vulnerable families identified through the SECC database.</p><h2>Coverage and Benefits</h2><p>The scheme covers up to Rs 5 lakh per family per year for medical treatment. This includes hospitalization expenses, surgeries, diagnostic tests, medicines and follow-up care. Pre-existing diseases are covered from day one of the policy with no waiting period. The coverage is cashless at all empaneled public and private hospitals across India. Over 1,600 medical procedures are covered under the scheme.</p><h2>Eligibility</h2><p>The scheme is based on the SECC 2011 database. Families identified as deprived in rural areas and specified occupation categories in urban areas are eligible. There is no age limit or family size restriction. All family members including newborn babies are automatically covered. The scheme is portable across India meaning beneficiaries can get treatment in any empaneled hospital anywhere in the country.</p><h2>How to Get the Card</h2><p>Beneficiaries can check their eligibility by visiting pmjay.gov.in and clicking on Am I Eligible. If eligible, they can visit any empaneled hospital with their Aadhaar card. The hospital will verify the eligibility through the PMJAY portal and issue an e-card immediately. No physical card is required as the treatment can be availed using Aadhaar-based verification.</p><h2>Documents Required</h2><ul><li>Aadhaar Card of all family members</li><li>Ration Card</li><li>Mobile number</li></ul>', `eligibility`='<p>Families in SECC 2011 database as deprived rural or specified occupation in urban areas. No age limit. No family size restriction. Portable across India. All family members covered including newborns.</p>', `benefits`='<p>Rs 5 lakh per family per year cashless health cover. 1,600+ medical procedures covered. Pre-existing diseases covered from day one. No cap on family size. Cashless treatment at 24,000+ empaneled hospitals across India.</p>', `application_process`='<p>Check eligibility at pmjay.gov.in. Visit empaneled hospital with Aadhaar. Hospital verifies eligibility on PMJAY portal. E-card issued immediately. Treatment can be availed with Aadhaar verification alone.</p>', `required_documents`='<ul><li>Aadhaar Card</li><li>Ration Card</li><li>Mobile Number</li></ul>' WHERE `slug`='ayushman-bharat-pmjay';
UPDATE schemes SET `content`='<p>Janani Suraksha Yojana (JSY) is a safe motherhood scheme under the National Health Mission. It provides cash assistance to pregnant women for institutional delivery.</p>
<h3>Cash Assistance</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>Low performing states:</strong> ₹1,400 (rural), ₹1,000 (urban)</li>
<li><strong>High performing states:</strong> ₹700 (rural), ₹600 (urban)</li>
</ul>
<h3>Additional Benefits</h3>
<ul>
<li>Free delivery at government health facilities</li>
<li>Free transport to health facility</li>
<li>Free diet during stay</li>
</ul>', `eligibility`='Pregnant women belonging to BPL/SC/ST households. Age 19+ years. For institutional delivery only.', `benefits`='₹600-1,400 cash assistance for institutional delivery, free delivery, free transport, free diet.', `application_process`='1. Register at nearest Sub-Centre or Health Facility during pregnancy\n2. Get Mother-Child Protection (MCP) card\n3. Deliver at government health facility or empanelled private hospital\n4. Claim cash assistance after delivery', `required_documents`='BPL Certificate, Aadhaar Card, MCP Card, Bank account details' WHERE `slug`='janani-suraksha-yojana';
UPDATE schemes SET `content`='<p>Mahatma Gandhi National Rural Employment Guarantee Act (MGNREGA) is a landmark social security scheme launched in 2005 by the Ministry of Rural Development. The scheme guarantees 100 days of wage employment per year to every rural household whose adult members volunteer for unskilled manual work. It is one of the largest work guarantee programs in the world.</p><h2>Key Features</h2><p>Employment is provided within 15 days of application. If employment is not provided, unemployment allowance must be paid. Wages are paid as per the minimum wage rate fixed by the central government, with different rates for different states. At least one-third of workers must be women.</p><h2>Eligibility</h2><p>All rural households are eligible. Adult members (18+ years) who are willing to do unskilled manual work can apply. Both men and women are eligible. No minimum education requirement.</p><h2>Benefits</h2><p>100 days guaranteed employment per household per year. Wages paid weekly through DBT. Works include water conservation, drought proofing, flood control, rural connectivity and land development. Worksite facilities include drinking water, shade and first aid.</p>', `eligibility`='<p>All adult rural household members (18+ years). Willing to do unskilled manual work. No education requirement. Priority to women (33% reservation).</p>', `benefits`='<p>100 days work per year per household. Weekly wage payment via DBT. Unemployment allowance if work not provided within 15 days. Worksite facilities provided.</p>', `application_process`='<p>Apply at local Gram Panchayat office. Fill Form A with basic details. Job Card issued within 15 days. Submit work request when employment needed.</p>', `required_documents`='<ul><li>Aadhaar Card</li><li>Residence Proof</li><li>Bank Account</li><li>Passport Photo</li><li>Family Member Details</li></ul>' WHERE `slug`='mgnrega';
UPDATE schemes SET `content`='<p>Pradhan Mantri Mudra Yojana (PMMY) is a flagship scheme launched in 2015 by the Ministry of Finance to provide loans up to Rs 10 lakh to non-corporate, non-farm small and micro entrepreneurs. The scheme enables small business owners to access affordable credit from banks for their income-generating activities.</p><h2>Three Categories</h2><p>The scheme offers three loan categories: Shishu (loans up to Rs 50,000 for start-ups), Kishore (Rs 50,001 to Rs 5 lakh for established businesses) and Tarun (Rs 5,00,001 to Rs 10 lakh for growing enterprises). Each category has different documentation and repayment terms.</p><h2>Eligibility</h2><p>Small entrepreneurs, artisans, traders, service providers and small business owners are eligible. The scheme covers manufacturing, processing, trading and service sector businesses. No collateral required for loans up to Rs 10 lakh under MUDRA.</p><h2>Benefits</h2><p>Collateral-free loans up to Rs 10 lakh. Affordable interest rates. Flexible repayment options. Doorstep banking through bank Mitras. Priority sector lending classification.</p>', `eligibility`='<p>Small entrepreneurs, artisans, traders, service providers. Non-corporate, non-farm businesses. Manufacturing, processing, trading and service sectors.</p>', `benefits`='<p>Collateral-free loans up to Rs 10 lakh. Three categories: Shishu (50K), Kishore (5L), Tarun (10L). Affordable interest rates. Priority sector status. Flexible repayment.</p>', `application_process`='<p>Apply at any bank branch or through online portal. Submit business plan and identity documents. Bank evaluates creditworthiness and sanctions loan amount.</p>', `required_documents`='<ul><li>Aadhaar Card</li><li>Business Plan</li><li>Bank Account</li><li>Identity Proof</li><li>Address Proof</li></ul>' WHERE `slug`='pm-mudra-yojana';
UPDATE schemes SET `content`='<p>Stand-Up India Scheme was launched in 2016 to facilitate bank loans between ₹10 lakh to ₹1 crore to at least one SC/ST borrower and at least one woman borrower per bank branch for setting up greenfield enterprises.</p>
<h3>Loan Details</h3>
<ul>
<li>Loan amount: ₹10 lakh to ₹1 crore</li>
<li>Composite loan covering 85% of project cost</li>
<li>Tenor: 7 years with moratorium period of 18 months</li>
<li>Interest rate: Base rate + 3% + Tenor premium</li>
</ul>', `eligibility`='SC/ST women entrepreneurs, or women entrepreneurs. Must be 18+ years. Enterprise must be greenfield (new venture). Must not be in default to any bank.', `benefits`='Loan ₹10 lakh to ₹1 crore, 85% project cost financing, 18 months moratorium, handholding support.', `application_process`='1. Visit standupmitra.in portal\n2. Register and fill application\n3. Submit business plan\n4. Bank processes and sanctions loan\n5. Handholding support through journey', `required_documents`='Aadhaar Card, Caste Certificate (for SC/ST), Business plan, Education/Experience certificates, Address proof' WHERE `slug`='stand-up-india-scheme';
UPDATE schemes SET `content`='<p>PM Rozgar Yojana provides employment opportunities to educated unemployed youth by facilitating self-employment through industry, business, service, and farm sector ventures.</p>', `eligibility`='Educated unemployed youth aged 18-35 years (SC/ST: 18-40 years). Minimum 8th pass. Family income below ₹40,000 per annum.', `benefits`='Subsidized loans for self-employment ventures, skill training, marketing support.', `application_process`='1. Apply through District Industries Centre\n2. Entrepreneurship training\n3. Project report preparation\n4. Bank loan processing', `required_documents`='Educational certificates, Aadhaar Card, Income Certificate, Caste Certificate (if applicable), Project report' WHERE `slug`='pradhan-mantri-rozgar-yojana';
UPDATE schemes SET `content`='<p>Pradhan Mantri Jan Dhan Yojana (PMJDY) is a national mission for financial inclusion launched by Prime Minister Narendra Modi on August 28, 2014. The scheme is under the Ministry of Finance and aims to provide comprehensive banking services to every unbanked household in India. It is one of the largest financial inclusion initiatives in the world, providing zero balance bank accounts with a RuPay debit card, accident insurance cover and overdraft facility.</p><h2>Key Features</h2><p>The scheme offers zero balance savings bank accounts with no minimum balance requirement. Each account holder receives a RuPay debit card with free insurance coverage. Accident insurance cover of Rs 2 lakh is provided to the cardholder. After six months of satisfactory operation, account holders become eligible for an overdraft facility of up to Rs 10,000. Life insurance cover of Rs 30,000 is also available for eligible account holders.</p><h2>Eligibility</h2><p>Any Indian citizen above 10 years of age is eligible to open an account under PMJDY. One account per person is allowed. There is no minimum balance requirement making it accessible to the poorest citizens. The scheme targets previously unbanked households and individuals.</p><h2>Benefits and Impact</h2><p>The scheme has brought millions of unbanked Indians into the formal banking system. It has enabled direct transfer of government subsidies and benefits to beneficiaries accounts, reducing leakages and corruption. The RuPay card allows cashless transactions and access to banking services anywhere in India.</p><h2>How to Open an Account</h2><p>Visit any bank branch with your Aadhaar card. Fill the simple account opening form. The bank official will complete the verification using your Aadhaar and issue the RuPay card immediately. Banking Correspondents (BCs) also visit villages to open accounts for rural residents who cannot visit bank branches.</p><h2>Documents Required</h2><ul><li>Aadhaar Card (accepted as both identity and address proof)</li><li>Passport size photograph</li><li>Mobile number</li></ul>', `eligibility`='<p>Any Indian citizen above 10 years. One account per person. No minimum balance required. All income groups eligible. Previously unbanked households prioritized.</p>', `benefits`='<p>Zero balance account. RuPay debit card with Rs 2 lakh accident insurance. Overdraft up to Rs 10,000 after 6 months. Life insurance cover of Rs 30,000. Direct benefit transfer facility. Mobile banking access.</p>', `application_process`='<p>Visit any bank branch or Banking Correspondent (BC) with Aadhaar card. Fill account opening form. Complete Aadhaar-based eKYC verification. Account opened immediately. RuPay card issued on the spot or delivered within a week.</p>', `required_documents`='<ul><li>Aadhaar Card</li><li>Passport size photograph</li><li>Mobile number</li></ul>' WHERE `slug`='pm-jan-dhan-yojana';
UPDATE schemes SET `content`='<h2>Atal Pension Yojana</h2><p>Guaranteed pension of ₹1,000-₹5,000/month for unorganised sector.</p>', `eligibility`='• Age 18-40 years
• Bank account holder
• Not covered by any pension scheme', `benefits`='• ₹1,000-₹5,000 monthly pension after 60
• Government co-contribution
